      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MOONRAKER (2) battled away for fifth in a stronger field at Geelong nearly 4 weeks ago, and before that he had been in good form at this level over 1100m. The extra 100m is a query, but he still looks to have an edge over his rivals in this. SUPREME THUNDER (3) resumes from a spell over a trip that is short of his best, but this veteran does come to hand quickly, and has not had any public trials, so he should be ready to rumble fresh up. MELISSA KATE (7) is a very durable local veteran mare, who was not at her best here last time out, and the fence that day was not really the place to be. She can make amends in this field, so stick with her. LADY MEMPHIS (6) will find this easier than her last start, and she is worth another chance. PORT LOUIS (1) improves with racing, and strips fitter here.",
